				\begin{document}$${L}_{1}\left({{{{z}}}}{{{{{\mathscr{,}}}}}}G\right)=\frac{1}{P\times Q}\mathop{\sum}\limits_{p}\mathop{\sum}\limits_{q}{{{{{\rm{|}}}}}}{{{{{z}}}}}_{p,q}-{G({x}_{{{{{{\rm{input}}}}}}})}_{p,q}{{{{{\rm{|}}}}}}$$\end{document}L1z,G=1P×Q∑p∑q∣zp,q−G(xinput)p,q∣where p and q are the pixel indices and P and Q are the total number of pixels in each image. The total variation loss is defined as:3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
